<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>
Zero-shot test R<sup id="S4.T2.3" class="ltx_sup">2</sup> (%) for <math id="S4.T2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> regression tasks.
Higher is better.
Global mean baseline is <math id="S4.T2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Setup is same as Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4.3 Zero-shot prompting ‣ 4 Results ‣ Relational Transformer: Toward Zero-Shot Foundation Models for Relational Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
LLM baselines are poor (App. <a href="#A7.SS2" title="G.2 Regression results with LLM baselines ‣ Appendix G Baseline Implementations ‣ Relational Transformer: Toward Zero-Shot Foundation Models for Relational Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.2</span></a>).
